{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162261-idigam-chronicle-changing-breeds","id":162261,"title":"Idigam Chronicle Changing Breeds","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-07T23:31:01-07:00","id":162261,"title":"Idigam Chronicle Changing Breeds","content":"I know that other Changing Breeds are outside scope of <b>Idigam Chronicle</b>. But looking on changes to this time, and what we know from <b>Changing Breeds</b> book - what adjustment would be needed in new take on Breeds? I ask as I want to add Ursara ( werebear ) character to our testing <b>IC </b>game and some mechanical guidelines would be in order. I assume that rules and modifiers would be to make every Breed based on sum of stats the Uratha have in they forms and <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-red-mist-descends/\" target=\"_blank\">two versions of Death Rage</a> would be give also to other races. What other changes would be needed? And what modifiers would Brown Bear changer have now? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T23:39:23-07:00","id":162275,"title":"","content":"You are a brave man, sir, to mention <b>Changing Breeds</b> on the WtF forum. For your werebear, you might be better off looking at <b>War Against the Pure</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T02:27:40-07:00","id":162307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162261-idigam-chronicle-changing-breeds?p=162275#post162275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are a brave man, sir, to mention <b>Changing Breeds</b> on the WtF forum.</div> </div> </div> </div>We, the Werehamsters, are a brave ( or foolish ) Breed! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.wizards.com/dnd/images/intheworks_20090302.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162261-idigam-chronicle-changing-breeds?p=162275#post162275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For your werebear, you might be better off looking at <b>War Against the Pure</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I looked, and I'm not satisfied. Yes, the <b>WAtP</b> has better balanced mechanics ( it HAS balanced mechanics ) and it's more opened ended on interpretation, but they Breeds are just so... blunt. Not to mentioned they don't have any werebears in compared to <b>Changing Breeds</b>. The ideal shifters book would be one with mechanics and openness of <b>WAtP</b> and fluff material of <b>Changing Breeds</b> for me. Not to mentioned that myself, I could add other weaknesses to shifters template, like Corax being vulnerable to <b>both</b> Silver and Gold.<br /> <br /> As to shifters stats, I will look in to them more closely later, maybe tomorrow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T05:03:34-07:00","id":162361,"title":"","content":"I remembered now about this great project on this topic...<br /> <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/33067-ancients-awaken-the-old-ones-chronicles-changing-breeds-discussion-brainstorming\">Ancients Awaken- the Old Ones Chronicles (Changing Breeds)</a></b><br /><br /><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Old Ones are presented in the small paragraph in the beginning of the first chapter. They are things which have came from before the First ones, before the very first beasts and man. While they seem to be hinted to be the dinosaurs, it isn't the first time rumors have been proved to be false. For this project's premise, the Old Ones are proto-beasts, things which are natural disasters in physical form. They are chatonic beings, like the Python which sleeps under Delphi or the Nidhog which sits at the bottom of the World's Tree. They are the enemies of all life, gathering cults around them and shape their surroundings.<br /> <br /> On the other side, there is humanity, which sometimes mess up with things they shouldn't and harms the world. But in the end, Nature always wins, and if humanity will keep in its destructive way Nature will take care of them by herself. Humanity is not, and never was, a threat for Nature, in the same way that an ant is not a threat to a man. Those Changing Folk who try to stop pollution and fight against the destruction of the landscape do so for humanity's sake. After all, the Changing Breeds exist in order to bridge between humanity and Nature. The Old Ones, however, work against that balance by their very existence, and as such they should be hunted down.<br /> <br /> Except of reversing the fluff, mechanics will also be updates. breeds will be turned into a real X splat so all of the changing breeds will feel like they belong to the same template, and accords may be changed a little. Virtue and Vice may be replaced with something which represent their inner beasts, and so does Harmony and Feral Heart. Favors and Aspects will be reworked, especially Beast's Magic and those which allow buying Gifts and/or Numina which will be replaced in a new &quot;sorcery system&quot;. Connections to the Shadow and the spirit world, both mechanically and fluff, will be removed, making the changing breeds based purely in the world of flesh. Forms will also be fixed, although that is in the bottom of the list. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T09:11:34-07:00","id":162440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162261-idigam-chronicle-changing-breeds?p=162275#post162275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are a brave man, sir, to mention <b>Changing Breeds</b> on the WtF forum. For your werebear, you might be better off looking at <b>War Against the Pure</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would have to agree with Weaver on this one, no offense sir hamster lol. Even if the Changing Breeds book was as balanced as WAtP ( which it wasn't, as you already know lol) the fluff for that book was just... bad. Sure it was more colorful than the fluff for the shifters in WAtP, but then again the tone of the book was much more blunt, thus it makes sense why their sections would be less colorful. But if I have to give examples of the slightly worse than bad fluff, I think I speak for many when I bring up the Royal Apes, Spinner-kin, The Pack mostly, and the Wind-Runners. Now some, like a couple Bastet, the Land Titans, and the Ursara were okay, as a whole the book was just.. blah in my opinion. Despite that, I do agree a compromise between the books could work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T09:22:43-07:00","id":162445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162261-idigam-chronicle-changing-breeds?p=162440#post162440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would have to agree with Weaver on this one, no offense sir hamster lol. Even if the Changing Breeds book was as balanced as WAtP ( which it wasn't, as you already know lol) the fluff for that book was just... bad. Sure it was more colorful than the fluff for the shifters in WAtP, but then again the tone of the book was much more blunt, thus it makes sense why their sections would be less colorful. But if I have to give examples of the slightly worse than bad fluff, I think I speak for many when I bring up the Royal Apes, Spinner-kin, The Pack mostly, and the Wind-Runners. Now some, like a couple Bastet, the Land Titans, and the Ursara were okay, as a whole the book was just.. blah in my opinion. Despite that, I do agree a compromise between the books could work.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> He may have meant that there was fluff for the different breeds, not the whole OWoD eco-terrorist bullshit that pervaded the book as a whole.<br /> <br /> Its one of the few books that I wish would be completely redone outside of the core-books. I feel that it is something people are interested in enough to want a rework of it, I just hope they don't go the same route with themes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T09:32:49-07:00","id":162472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162261-idigam-chronicle-changing-breeds?p=162445#post162445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> He may have meant that there was fluff for the different breeds, not the whole OWoD eco-terrorist bullshit that pervaded the book as a whole.<br /> <br /> Its one of the few books that I wish would be completely redone outside of the core-books. I feel that it is something people are interested in enough to want a rework of it, I just hope they don't go the same route with themes.</div> </div> </div> </div>EXACTLY what I was thinking. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}